---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';

const activities = [
	{
		key: 'vig',
		name: 'Vigorous physical activities',
		daysQ: 'During the last 7 days, on how many days did you do vigorous physical activities like heavy lifting, digging, aerobics, or fast bicycling?',
		timeQ: 'How much time did you usually spend doing vigorous physical activities on one of those days?',
		help: 'Vigorous activities take hard physical effort and make you breathe much harder than normal. Only count activities you did for at least 10 minutes at a time.',
		met: 8.0,
	},
	{
		key: 'mod',
		name: 'Moderate physical activities',
		daysQ: 'During the last 7 days, on how many days did you do moderate physical activities like carrying light loads, bicycling at a regular pace, or doubles tennis? Do not include walking.',
		timeQ: 'How much time did you usually spend doing moderate physical activities on one of those days?',
		help: 'Moderate activities take moderate physical effort and make you breathe somewhat harder than normal. Only count activities you did for at least 10 minutes at a time.',
		met: 4.0,
	},
	{
		key: 'walk',
		name: 'Walking',
		daysQ: 'During the last 7 days, on how many days did you walk for at least 10 minutes at a time?',
		timeQ: 'How much time did you usually spend walking on one of those days?',
		help: 'Include walking at work and at home, walking to travel from place to place, and any other walking done solely for recreation, sport, exercise or leisure.',
		met: 3.3,
	},
];
---

<Page
	title="IPAQ short form: free online physical activity questionnaire with scoring"
	description="Complete the International Physical Activity Questionnaire (IPAQ) short form online and get your MET-minutes per week and activity category instantly. Seven questions about the last 7 days. Free, no sign-up required."
>
	<Fragment slot="head">
			<script type="application/ld+json">
	{
	  "@context": "https://schema.org",
	  "@graph": [
	    {
	      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
	      "itemListElement": [
	        {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://www.postviralrecovery.com/"},
	        {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Tools", "item": "https://www.postviralrecovery.com/tools/"},
	        {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "IPAQ short form", "item": "https://www.postviralrecovery.com/tools/ipaq-short-form/"}
	      ]
	    },
	    {
	      "@type": "FAQPage",
	      "mainEntity": [
	        {
	          "@type": "Question",
	          "name": "What is the IPAQ short form?",
	          "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The International Physical Activity Questionnaire short form is a seven-item measure of physical activity over the last 7 days, developed by an international group in the late 1990s and validated across 12 countries. It asks about days and minutes of vigorous activity, moderate activity and walking, plus time spent sitting. The answers are converted to MET-minutes per week and a category of low, moderate or high activity. It is free to use."}
	        },
	        {
	          "@type": "Question",
	          "name": "What do MET-minutes mean?",
	          "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "A MET is a multiple of resting energy expenditure. The IPAQ assigns walking 3.3 METs, moderate activity 4 METs and vigorous activity 8 METs, and multiplies each by the minutes per day and days per week. A total of 600 MET-minutes a week corresponds roughly to the public-health guideline of 150 minutes of moderate activity."}
	        },
	        {
	          "@type": "Question",
	          "name": "Is a low IPAQ category a bad result if I have a post-viral condition?",
	          "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Not in itself. The categories were built for the general population. In ME/CFS, POTS and long COVID with post-exertional malaise, the safe level of activity is whatever does not trigger a crash, and the low category is where many people need to be. The value of the questionnaire is as a record over time and as an honest account of activity for a clinician, including sitting time, which the other measures ignore."}
	        }
	      ]
	    }
	  ]
	}
			</script>
	</Fragment>
			<div class="tool-header">
				<a href="/tools" class="section-label tools">Tools</a>
				<h1>IPAQ short form</h1>
				<p class="subtitle">Seven questions about the last 7 days, scored in MET-minutes per week</p>
				<p class="description">
					The International Physical Activity Questionnaire was developed in the late 1990s by a group of researchers convened by the World Health Organization, to give a comparable measure of physical activity across countries. The short form asks about the last 7 days: how many days and how long you did vigorous activity, moderate activity and walking, and how long you spent sitting on a weekday. It was validated in 12 countries and is one of the most used physical activity questionnaires in research. Its scoring converts your answers to MET-minutes per week and a category of low, moderate or high.
				</p>
				<p class="description">
					For post-viral conditions the IPAQ has two things going for it. It counts walking and everyday effort rather than only exercise, which is where most of a limited energy budget goes. And it records sitting time, which nothing else on this site does. It is offered here as a record, not a target: the categories were built for healthy adults, and in a condition with post-exertional malaise the low category is often the right place to be. What the score is good for is watching your own trend, and giving a clinician an honest account of your activity level instead of a guess. The <a href="/tools/godin-shephard-leisure-time-exercise-questionnaire/">Godin-Shephard questionnaire</a> is a one-minute alternative that counts only leisure exercise.
				</p>
				<div class="disclaimer">
					<strong>This is not a diagnostic tool or an exercise prescription.</strong> It records what you did last week; it does not say what you should do. If you have post-exertional malaise, see the <a href="/tools/exercise-readiness/">exercise readiness screen</a> before changing your activity. Source: Craig CL, Marshall AL, Sjöström M, et al. <em>International physical activity questionnaire: 12-country reliability and validity.</em> Med Sci Sports Exerc. 2003;35(8):1381–1395. Scoring follows the <em>Guidelines for Data Processing and Analysis of the IPAQ</em>, November 2005. The IPAQ is freely available for use without permission and is reproduced here with attribution.
				</div>
			</div>

			<form id="ipaq-form" novalidate>
				<p class="form-instructions">Think about all the activities you did in the <strong>last 7 days</strong>: at work, at home, travelling from place to place, and in your spare time for recreation, exercise or sport. Only count activities you did for <strong>at least 10 minutes at a time</strong>. Enter 0 days if you did none of that kind.</p>

				<div class="question-grid">
					{activities.map((a, i) => (
						<div class="question" data-index={i}>
							<p class="q-head">{a.name}</p>
							<p class="q-help">{a.help}</p>
							<p class="q-text"><span class="q-num">{i * 2 + 1}.</span> {a.daysQ}</p>
							<label class="count-label">
								<input type="number" id={`${a.key}-days`} min="0" max="7" step="1" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="0" /> days per week
							</label>
							<p class="q-text"><span class="q-num">{i * 2 + 2}.</span> {a.timeQ}</p>
							<div class="time-row">
								<label class="count-label"><input type="number" id={`${a.key}-hours`} min="0" max="16" step="1" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="0" /> hours</label>
								<label class="count-label"><input type="number" id={`${a.key}-mins`} min="0" max="59" step="1" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="0" /> minutes per day</label>
							</div>
						</div>
					))}

					<div class="question" data-index="3">
						<p class="q-head">Sitting</p>
						<p class="q-help">Include time spent sitting at a desk, visiting friends, reading, or sitting or lying down to watch television. Do not include time asleep.</p>
						<p class="q-text"><span class="q-num">7.</span> During the last 7 days, how much time did you spend sitting on a week day?</p>
						<div class="time-row">
							<label class="count-label"><input type="number" id="sit-hours" min="0" max="24" step="1" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="0" /> hours</label>
							<label class="count-label"><input type="number" id="sit-mins" min="0" max="59" step="1" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="0" /> minutes per day</label>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="form-footer">
					<button type="submit">Calculate score</button>
					<button type="button" id="reset-btn">Clear all</button>
				</div>
			</form>

			<div id="results" class="results" hidden>
				<h2>Your IPAQ result</h2>
				<div class="total-score">
					<span id="total-score-value">—</span>
					<span class="total-score-label">MET-minutes per week</span>
				</div>
				<p id="score-interpretation" class="score-interp"></p>
				<div id="breakdown" class="subscores"></div>
				<p id="notes" class="calc-notes"></p>

				<div class="results-disclaimer">
					<h3>Understanding your result</h3>
					<p>Each kind of activity is converted to MET-minutes: minutes per day, multiplied by days per week, multiplied by an intensity weight of <strong>3.3</strong> for walking, <strong>4.0</strong> for moderate activity and <strong>8.0</strong> for vigorous activity. The three are added to give a weekly total. Following the IPAQ scoring guidelines, any activity under 10 minutes a day is treated as 0, and each activity is capped at 180 minutes a day before scoring, so a single very long day does not swamp the week.</p>
					<p>The categories are: <strong>high</strong>, meaning vigorous activity on at least 3 days reaching 1500 MET-minutes, or any combination on all 7 days reaching 3000 MET-minutes; <strong>moderate</strong>, meaning vigorous activity of at least 20 minutes on 3 or more days, or moderate activity or walking of at least 30 minutes on 5 or more days, or any combination on 5 or more days reaching 600 MET-minutes; and <strong>low</strong> for everything else. The 600 figure corresponds roughly to the 150-minutes-a-week public-health guideline.</p>
					<p>Those categories were designed for healthy populations. In ME/CFS, POTS or long COVID with post-exertional malaise, a low category is frequently the correct and safe level, and pushing toward "moderate" is how many people crash. Read the number as a description of last week, compare it with your own earlier weeks, and set it next to how you felt afterwards. Sitting time is reported separately and is not part of the activity score; in orthostatic conditions, time spent sitting or lying is often a deliberate management choice.</p>
					<p><strong>This is not an exercise prescription.</strong> If you are considering changing your activity level, start with the <a href="/tools/exercise-readiness/">readiness screen</a> and the <a href="/tools/pacing-and-heart-rate/">pacing guide</a>, and let your clinician's advice outrank any questionnaire.</p>
				</div>

				<button type="button" id="back-btn" class="back-btn">Edit answers</button>
			</div>
</Page>

<script>
const form = document.getElementById('ipaq-form') as HTMLFormElement;
const results = document.getElementById('results') as HTMLElement;

function flag(index: number, el: HTMLInputElement) {
	const q = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`.question[data-index="${index}"]`);
	q?.classList.add('missing');
	q?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
	setTimeout(() => q?.classList.remove('missing'), 2500);
	el.focus();
}

function num(id: string, max: number, index: number): number | null {
	const el = document.getElementById(id) as HTMLInputElement;
	const raw = el.value.trim();
	const n = raw === '' ? 0 : parseInt(raw, 10);
	if (!Number.isFinite(n) || n < 0 || n > max) { flag(index, el); return null; }
	return n;
}

form.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
	e.preventDefault();

	const keys = [['vig', 8.0, 'Vigorous'], ['mod', 4.0, 'Moderate'], ['walk', 3.3, 'Walking']] as [string, number, string][];
	const parts: { name: string; days: number; mins: number; scoredMins: number; met: number }[] = [];
	const notes: string[] = [];
	let rawTotalMinutes = 0;

	for (let i = 0; i < keys.length; i++) {
		const [k, met, name] = keys[i];
		const days = num(`${k}-days`, 7, i); if (days === null) return;
		const h = num(`${k}-hours`, 16, i); if (h === null) return;
		const m = num(`${k}-mins`, 59, i); if (m === null) return;
		let mins = h * 60 + m;
		if (days > 0 && mins > 0 && mins < 10) { notes.push(`${name}: under 10 minutes a day, so counted as 0 per the IPAQ rules.`); mins = 0; }
		let scoredMins = mins;
		if (scoredMins > 180) { notes.push(`${name}: ${mins} minutes a day capped at 180 for scoring.`); scoredMins = 180; }
		const effDays = mins > 0 ? days : 0;
		rawTotalMinutes += mins;
		parts.push({ name, days: effDays, mins, scoredMins, met: Math.round(met * scoredMins * effDays) });
	}
	const sitH = num('sit-hours', 24, 3); if (sitH === null) return;
	const sitM = num('sit-mins', 59, 3); if (sitM === null) return;
	const sitting = sitH * 60 + sitM;

	if (rawTotalMinutes > 960) {
		notes.push('Your reported activity adds up to more than 16 hours a day. The IPAQ guidelines treat such records as unreliable; the total below is shown for completeness but the category is not assigned.');
	}

	const [vig, mod, walk] = parts;
	const total = vig.met + mod.met + walk.met;
	const anyDays = Math.min(7, vig.days + mod.days + walk.days);
	// Days of moderate activity or walking that themselves reached 30 minutes.
	const thirtyMinDays = Math.min(7, (mod.scoredMins >= 30 ? mod.days : 0) + (walk.scoredMins >= 30 ? walk.days : 0));

	let category: string;
	if (rawTotalMinutes > 960) category = 'not assigned';
	else if ((vig.days >= 3 && vig.met >= 1500) || (anyDays >= 7 && total >= 3000)) category = 'high';
	else if (
		(vig.days >= 3 && vig.scoredMins >= 20) ||
		thirtyMinDays >= 5 ||
		(anyDays >= 5 && total >= 600)
	) category = 'moderate';
	else category = 'low';

	(document.getElementById('total-score-value') as HTMLElement).textContent = String(total);

	let note: string;
	if (category === 'high') {
		note = 'Your activity last week met the IPAQ threshold for the high category, which in general-population terms is well above the public-health guideline. If you have a post-exertional condition, the meaningful question is what the days after that week were like.';
	} else if (category === 'moderate') {
		note = 'Your activity last week met the IPAQ threshold for the moderate category, roughly in line with the 150-minutes-a-week guideline for healthy adults. For someone managing a limited energy envelope, holding this steady without a flare matters more than moving up a category.';
	} else if (category === 'low') {
		note = 'Your activity last week fell below the IPAQ moderate threshold. For a healthy adult that would be a prompt to move more. For someone with ME/CFS, POTS or long COVID it is very often the right level, and the useful comparison is with your own earlier weeks and with how you felt afterwards, not with the general-population bands.';
	} else {
		note = 'The activity you entered adds up to more than 16 hours a day, which the IPAQ treats as an unreliable record. Check the hours and minutes fields and try again.';
	}
	(document.getElementById('score-interpretation') as HTMLElement).textContent =
		`Your total is ${total} MET-minutes per week, which places you in the IPAQ "${category}" activity category. ${note}`;

	const sitText = sitting > 0 ? `${Math.floor(sitting / 60)} h ${sitting % 60} min` : '0 min';
	(document.getElementById('breakdown') as HTMLElement).innerHTML = parts.map(p => `
		<div><span class="sub-label">${p.name}</span><span class="sub-value">${p.met} MET-min</span><span class="sub-detail">${p.days} day${p.days === 1 ? '' : 's'} × ${p.scoredMins} min</span></div>`).join('') +
		`<div><span class="sub-label">Sitting on a weekday</span><span class="sub-value">${sitText}</span><span class="sub-detail">not part of the activity score</span></div>`;

	(document.getElementById('notes') as HTMLElement).textContent = notes.join(' ');

	form.hidden = true;
	results.hidden = false;
	results.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
});

document.getElementById('reset-btn')?.addEventListener('click', () => form.reset());
document.getElementById('back-btn')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
	results.hidden = true;
	form.hidden = false;
	form.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
});
</script>

<style>
	.tool-header {
		padding-bottom: 1.5em;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		margin-bottom: 2.5em;
	}
	.tool-header h1 { margin: 0.3em 0 0.1em; }
	.subtitle { color: rgb(var(--gray)); font-size: 1.05em; margin: 0 0 0.75em; }
	.description { margin-bottom: 1em; }
	.disclaimer a { color: inherit; }

	.form-instructions {
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		font-style: italic;
		margin-bottom: 1.5em;
		font-size: 0.95em;
	}

	.question-grid { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0; }
	.question {
		padding: 1.25em 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
	}
	.question.missing { background: rgba(192, 57, 43, 0.05); border-radius: 6px; }
	.q-head { font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 0.2em; color: rgb(var(--black)); }
	.q-help { margin: 0 0 0.9em; font-size: 0.85em; color: rgb(var(--gray)); line-height: 1.5; }
	.q-text { margin: 0 0 0.5em; font-size: 0.95em; }
	.q-text + .count-label, .q-text + .time-row { margin-bottom: 1.1em; }
	.q-num { font-weight: 700; margin-right: 0.25em; }
	.time-row { display: flex; gap: 1em; flex-wrap: wrap; }
	.count-label { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6em; font-size: 0.88em; font-weight: 700; color: rgb(var(--gray-dark)); }
	.count-label input {
		width: 5em; padding: 0.5em; font-size: 1rem; font-family: inherit; font-weight: 400;
		border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); border-radius: 5px;
	}

	.form-footer { display: flex; gap: 1em; padding: 2em 0 1em; }
	button[type="submit"] {
		background: var(--accent); color: #fff; border: none;
		padding: 0.75em 2em; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 1em; font-weight: 700;
		cursor: pointer; font-family: inherit;
	}
	button[type="submit"]:hover { background: var(--accent-dark); }
	button[type="button"] {
		background: none; border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		padding: 0.75em 1.5em; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 0.95em;
		cursor: pointer; color: rgb(var(--gray)); font-family: inherit;
	}

	.results { padding-top: 1em; }
	.results h2 { margin-bottom: 0.5em; }
	.total-score { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.5em; margin: 1em 0; flex-wrap: wrap; }
	#total-score-value { font-size: 3.5em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); line-height: 1; }
	.total-score-label { color: rgb(var(--gray)); font-size: 1.1em; }
	.score-interp {
		font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 1.5em;
		padding: 1em 1.25em; background: var(--accent-light);
		border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 4px;
	}
	.subscores { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 0.75em; margin-bottom: 1em; }
	.subscores :global(div) { border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.7em 0.9em; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
	.subscores :global(.sub-label) { font-size: 0.75em; color: rgb(var(--gray)); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
	.subscores :global(.sub-value) { font-size: 1.15em; font-weight: 700; color: rgb(var(--black)); }
	.subscores :global(.sub-detail) { font-size: 0.78em; color: rgb(var(--gray)); }
	.calc-notes { font-size: 0.85em; color: rgb(var(--gray)); margin: 0 0 2em; }
	.calc-notes:empty { display: none; }
	.results-disclaimer {
		font-size: 0.88em;
		color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
		border-top: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		padding-top: 1.5em;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}
	.results-disclaimer h3 { font-size: 1em; color: rgb(var(--black)); margin-bottom: 0.5em; margin-top: 0; }
	.results-disclaimer a { color: var(--accent); }
	.back-btn {
		background: none;
		border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		padding: 0.6em 1.25em;
		border-radius: 5px;
		font-size: 0.95em;
		cursor: pointer;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		font-family: inherit;
		margin-top: 1em;
	}
	.back-btn:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }

	@media (max-width: 600px) {
		.form-footer { flex-direction: column; }
		.subscores { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
	}
</style>
